st kind of gave me  what's up uh listen back we could talk  to you all day but uh we appreciate you  being so generous with your time  last one for me is i just i know we're  in a pandemic and so you know and  obviously you know california especially  you know it's been uh most people been  you know inside and you know  on lockdown and rightfully so but is  there a great interaction  a great story even a great phone call  zoom meeting whatever  since you have been a world series  winning manager  that you can share with us i told you  before you got two cities now that  you'll never pay for a meal in  boston and l.a which is not bad it's  pretty good dining but since you brought  it home for the dodgers  give me your best story from the off  season  um the best um okay  so um we haven't had that chance to  celebrate yet  um and i'm still hoping for a laker  dodger  parade all throughout the city of uh los  angeles  you got a.d lebron coach vogel  and then you got kershaw bets all these  guys right  but i had a call from sandy koufax  which was just uh ridiculous  and just kind of congratulating me and  how we did it  uh vince scully uh is insane  um i just i've got so many of those like  random great people just hit me up  uh congratulating me so very humble very  blessed  man what a history what a history uh for  the dodgers  you know you you mentioned some of those  guys vin scully been there uh you know  sandy koufax  uh and and just like your story too i  and before we let you go i just want to  congratulate you because i wonder  if it started to play some mind games  with you you guys kept winning was it  eight straight  um division titles that you won yeah we  won eight straight so uh  you know we've earned that target on our  back that's what you play for right  so uh yeah and i expect to do it again  next year  um but you guys are the best and uh one  last thing is  you guys talked about what we can do for  uh as far as getting uh more black  players playing